TI  - Pirfenidone-induced Eosinophilic Pleurisy.
PG  - 1863-1866
LID - 10.2169/internalmedicine.56.7738 [doi]
AB  - The patient was a 69-year-old man with idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis who was 
      taking pirfenidone. After 7 weeks of treatment, he suffered from left-sided 
      eosinophilic pleurisy. Medical thoracoscopy was performed and the 
      histopathological examination of the parietal pleura revealed the massive 
      infiltration of eosinophils and lymphoid follicles. After stopping pirfenidone 
      therapy, the patient's pleural effusion disappeared without additional treatment, 
      and never recurred. This is the first case report of pirfenidone-induced 
      pleurisy.
