TI  - Medical thoracoscopy for the treatment of complicated hepatic hydrothorax.
PG  - 2
LID - 10.1093/jscr/2012.3.2 [doi]
AB  - Hepatic hydrothorax is a complication of liver cirrhosis. Several invasive 
      therapeutic approaches have been performed such as thoracentesis, video-assisted 
      thoracic surgery and repair of the diaphragmatic defects with debatable results. 
      Medical thoracoscopy is a minimally invasive and effective technique with 
      challenging applications that has not been thoroughly used in the treatment of 
      hepatic hydrothorax. We hereby present the case of a hepatic hydrothorax 
      complicated by thoracic empyema in a 38-year-old patient with alcoholic cirrhosis 
      that was treated with medical thoracoscopy and talc pleurodesis.
