DP  - 2014 Sep
TI  - Application of medical thoracoscopy in diagnosis of sarcoidosis-related pleural 
      effusion.
PG  - 99-101
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.62 [doi]
AB  - Pleural effusion caused by sarcoidosis is unusual. Medical thoracoscopy could 
      help clinicians detect associated pleural disease, yet studies on thoracoscopic 
      observations in sarcoidosis pleural involvement are rare. In this article, we 
      report the utility of medical thoracoscopy in diagnosing sarcoid-related pleural 
      disease for three patients. Pleural nodularity was common with solitary and 
      multiple nodules evident; biopsies confirmed the presence of diagnostic 
      noncaseating granulomas.
