TI  - Tuberculous pleurisy diagnosed by medical thoracoscopy in an adalimumab-treated 
      rheumatoid arthritis patient after treatment of latent tuberculosis infection.
PG  - 1013-7
LID - 10.1007/s10165-012-0727-5 [doi]
AB  - A 28-year-old rheumatoid arthritis woman treated with adalimumab was admitted 
      with fever, cough, and right chest pain. X-ray showed right pleural effusion. By 
      medical thoracoscopy, diffuse white nodules were observed, and biopsy specimen 
      demonstrated epithelioid cell granulomas with necrosis and auramine-stained 
      organisms, which suggested a diagnosis of tuberculous pleurisy. Medical 
      thoracoscopy can be a potent diagnostic method when tuberculous pleurisy is 
      suspected. Notably, despite latent tuberculosis treatment, active tuberculosis 
      was not prevented.
